      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2010 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Many pathological processes can present as a swelling in the groin. We present a case of complex, ruptured pyonephrosis causing a psoas collection, which in turn presented clinically as an apparent right \"incarcerated inguinal hernia.\" The patient was successfully treated with antibiotics and ultrasound-guided drainage of the abscess. The anatomical basis of the inguinal presentation of this complex pyonephrosis can be understood in the arrangement of the renal (Gerota's) fascia."
      },
